set.body:
Handle general linear compositions for which prox(phi) does not imply prox(phi composed with T).

Families:
- graph total variation and fused lasso;
- overlapping groups through lifted variables;
- aligned-score l1, group, Huber, and bounded/equality targets;
- auxiliary-variable constraints z = T(theta).

Lowering options include ADMM, primal-dual, augmented-Lagrangian, or conic forms through explicit capability selection. Proximal and projection algorithms belong to functionals/sets and solver capabilities, not semantic map nodes.

Acceptance:
- KKT/primal-dual residual certificates;
- differential comparison with a trusted small convex solver/reference;
- overlapping groups never use the naive separable prox;
- stopping and infeasibility semantics are typed;
- JVM/JS reference path or an explicitly documented platform boundary with shared semantic tests.
